    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7yNO4e",
      "title": "feat: re-add OPCM V800 templates with simplified super-permissioned args",
      "author": "OptimismBot",
      "number": 1502,
      "body": "> **Draft — do not merge until the V800 OPCM is deployed on-chain.**\n\nRe-adds the `OPCMUpgradeV800` and `OPCMMigrateV800` templates, their integration tests, and example tasks that were removed in #1501, now carrying the simplified super-permissioned game arg layout from #1500.\n\nStacked on #1501 (base branch `centaur/remove-opcm-v800-templates`). GitHub will retarget this to `main` once #1501 merges.\n\n## What changed vs the original V800 templates\n`OPCMUpgradeV800` encodes `SUPER_PERMISSIONED_CANNON` (gt=5) game args as **proposer-only** (`abi.encode(a.proposer)`, 32 bytes) instead of the old `abi.encode(absolutePrestate, proposer, challenger)`, matching the simplified op-contracts V800 ABI. Test coverage in `SuperRootUpgrade.t.sol` is updated accordingly, and `test_upgrade_sepolia()` is dropped because the forked OPCM predates the new layout. This is the exact diff from #1500.\n\n## Why draft\nV800 is not yet deployed on-chain, so `template_regression_tests` cannot simulate `035-opcm-upgrade-v800` against a compatible OPCM — it reverts in `_build`. By removing the templates from `main` (#1501) and re-adding the new version here, we avoid carrying a backwards-compatibility shim for a not-yet-live OPCM. Once V800 is deployed: merge #1501, then mark this ready and merge.\n\nCloses #1466 (once merged)\n\nPrompted by: @mds1\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-15T20:34:18Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1652,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7xO-TZ",
      "title": "Allow new Safe owners to presign follow-up tasks",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1497,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an explicit `SKIP_SIGNER_OWNER_CHECK=true|1` override to the shared `TaskManager` signing preflight. This lets a new Safe owner presign a follow-up task before the earlier owner-addition task executes; the owner check remains enabled by default.\n\nThe bypass still rejects a zero signer or codeless target and calls `getOwners()` to validate the Safe interface. It skips only owner membership and prints a warning with the signer and Safe addresses. A recursive policy test rejects `SKIP_SIGNER_OWNER_CHECK` in every tracked task `.env`, so the exception stays command-scoped.\n\n## Why\n\nSequential owner rotations intentionally require a newly added owner to sign a later task. For example, `056-fus-rotation-1` adds an owner that must sign `057-fus-rotation-2`, but the existing preflight reads current onchain ownership and blocks that signature until `056` executes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `mise exec -- forge fmt --check`\n- `mise exec -- forge test --match-contract TaskManagerUnitTest --match-test 'test(RequireSignerOnSafe|TaskEnvFiles_DoNotContainSkipSignerOwnerCheck)' -vv` (`2/2` pass)\n- `FOUNDRY_PROFILE=ci mise exec -- forge build`\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check`\n- Independent spec/quality, security/operations, test, and whole-branch reviews completed with no open findings\n\n## Additional context\n\nThe override skips only the current-owner preflight. Simulation, transaction construction, hash validation, hardware-wallet signing, and execution-time signature validation are unchanged.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-13T19:35:05Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-07-14T16:42:46Z",
      "additions": 85,
      "deletions": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7xoVMT",
      "title": "fix: preserve Safe owners in simulation overrides",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1498,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nPreserve the Safe's real owner links when adding the synthetic simulation owner. The override now appends that owner and increments `ownerCount` instead of replacing the real owner list, which fixes Tenderly simulations that rotate the first owner.\n\nThis only changes simulation authentication state. The simulated list has one extra owner, but remains internally consistent; task calldata, Safe transaction hashes, signatures, and onchain state are unchanged. Tasks that depend on the exact owner count or enumerate owners still require a different simulation strategy.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `forge test --match-contract StateOverrideManagerUnitTest --match-test test_getStateOverrides_appendsSimulationOwnerWithoutReplacingOwnerList -vv`\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-14T15:51:53Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 71,
      "deletions": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7xpTuV",
      "title": "fix: simulate Safe tasks from an existing owner",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1499,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nUse an existing pre-execution Safe owner as the Tenderly simulation sender. This leaves the root Safe owner list and `ownerCount` unchanged, fixing first-owner rotations such as task 057.\n\nStacked simulations previously used an internal contract caller and made it a synthetic owner. Child Safe simulation overrides are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `mise exec -- forge fmt --check`\n- `mise exec -- forge build`\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-14T16:29:22Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-07-14T19:10:59Z",
      "additions": 17,
      "deletions": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7x2C5P",
      "title": "fix: simplify OPCM V800 super permissioned game args",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 1500,
      "body": "Updates `OPCMUpgradeV800` to encode `SUPER_PERMISSIONED_CANNON` game args as proposer-only, matching the simplified op-contracts ABI. Updates fork-backed config coverage and removes execution against the pre-change Sepolia OPCM fixture.\n\nCloses ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops#1466\n\nTest plan:\n- `forge build --deny-warnings`\n- `forge test --match-contract 'SuperRootUpgrade(Test|SetupValidationTest)' -vvv`\n- `forge fmt --check src/template/OPCMUpgradeV800.sol test/integration/SuperRootUpgrade.t.sol`\n- `./src/script/check-struct-order.sh`\n\nFull `forge test`: 299 passed; 2 unrelated integration tests require unavailable external/local RPC services.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-15T03:21:35Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 86
    }
